# A target bounded below by a negative literal (#147): {a: 0} gives -6, which
# >=-5 rejects. The bound is read, so the target is not taken as unbounded.
-- source.cue --
a: int & >=0 & <=10
-- target.cue --
n: int & >=-5 & <=5
-- lens.cue --
v0_0: _
v1_0: {n: v0_0.a - 6}
-- out --
not total
v1_0.n is v0_0.a - 6, which may be as low as -6, where the target schema requires >=-5 (rule computed-narrowed) @ lens.cue:2:11
